TUnit has four lifecycle scopes, each with `[Before(…)]` / `[After(…)]` attributes. Here's the full picture:

---

### 1. Per-test — `[Before(Test)]` / `[After(Test)]`

```csharp
public class OrderTests
{
    [Before(Test)]
    public void ResetDatabase(TestContext context)
    {
        // Runs before every [Test] in this class
        InMemoryDb.Reset();
    }

    [After(Test)]
    public void Cleanup(TestContext context)
    {
        // Runs after every [Test] in this class
    }

    [Test]
    public async Task Order_WithNoItems_Throws()
    {
        await Assert.That(() => new Order().Submit())
            .ThrowsExactly<InvalidOperationException>();
    }
}
```

*(A constructor + `IAsyncDisposable.DisposeAsync` also works for this scope.)*

---

### 2. Per-class — `[Before(Class)]` / `[After(Class)]`

```csharp
public class IntegrationTests
{
    private static TestFixture _fixture = null!;

    [Before(Class)]
    public static void OpenFixture(ClassHookContext context)
    {
        _fixture = new TestFixture();   // once before first test
    }

    [After(Class)]
    public static void DisposeFixture(ClassHookContext context)
    {
        _fixture.Dispose();             // once after last test
    }

    [Test]
    public async Task CanQuery() { /* use _fixture */ }
}
```

---

### 3. Per-assembly — `[Before(Assembly)]` / `[After(Assembly)]`

```csharp
public class WireMockHook
{
    [Before(Assembly)]
    public static void StartServer(AssemblyHookContext context)
    {
        WireMockServer.Start();         // once for the whole assembly
    }

    [After(Assembly)]
    public static void StopServer(AssemblyHookContext context)
    {
        WireMockServer.Stop();
    }
}
```

---

### 4. Per-session (entire test run) — `[Before(TestSession)]` / `[After(TestSession)]`

```csharp
public class GlobalSetup
{
    [Before(TestSession)]
    public static void ApplyMigrations(TestSessionContext context)
    {
        Database.Migrate();             // once at the very start
    }

    [After(TestSession)]
    public static void TearDown(TestSessionContext context)
    {
        Database.Drop();                // once at the very end
    }
}
```

---

### Quick-reference table

| Scope | Before | After | Context param |
|---|---|---|---|
| Each test | `[Before(Test)]` | `[After(Test)]` | `TestContext` |
| Class | `[Before(Class)]` | `[After(Class)]` | `ClassHookContext` |
| Assembly | `[Before(Assembly)]` | `[After(Assembly)]` | `AssemblyHookContext` |
| Session | `[Before(TestSession)]` | `[After(TestSession)]` | `TestSessionContext` |

**Bonus:** `[BeforeEvery(Test)]` / `[AfterEvery(Test)]` (and `Class`/`Assembly` variants) are *global* hooks — they fire for every test/class/assembly across the run, useful for cross-cutting concerns like logging. The context parameter and `CancellationToken` are optional on all hooks.
